# PROJECT AT A GLANCE

The Library Book Inventory and Search System is a simple command-line project developed using basic Ubuntu/Linux commands. It helps organise a small library catalogue, search for books by title or category, separate available and issued books, and prepare an inventory report.

**Main Operations:**

1. STORE – Store book details.
2. SEARCH – Find books by title.
3. FILTER – Separate available and issued books.
4. REPORT – Generate an inventory report.

**Tools Used:** mkdir, cd, touch, echo, grep, cut, sort, cat, head, tail and less.

---

# 1. INTRODUCTION

A small library may maintain its book catalogue in notebooks or separate lists. When a student asks for a particular title, category, or book availability, the librarian may need to check several entries manually. This can take time, especially when the collection grows.

The Library Book Inventory and Search System is a simple file-based project. It stores book details in text files and uses Linux commands to search, filter, extract, sort, display, and combine catalogue entries.

This project uses only basic Linux commands without any programming language, database, or shell script.

# 2. PROBLEM STATEMENT

In a small college library, book details and their issue status may be recorded manually. Searching for a title, identifying available books, separating issued books, and preparing an inventory list can become repetitive and may lead to mistakes.

The main problem is to organise a basic book catalogue and make common search and reporting tasks easier using Linux commands.

# 3. WHAT WE ARE GOING TO DO

We will create a folder-based catalogue containing one main file, two filtered files, and two report files.

| File / Folder | Purpose |
|---|---|
| data/books.txt | Main catalogue containing 10 sample book records. |
| data/available.txt | Stores books whose status is Available. |
| data/issued.txt | Stores books whose status is Issued. |
| reports/sorted_books.txt | Catalogue sorted alphabetically by book title. |
| reports/final_inventory.txt | Combined available and issued-book report. |

**Book Record Format:**

Book_ID,Title,Author,Category,Status

**Example:**

B101,The Alchemist,Paulo Coelho,Fiction,Available

# 4. HOW WE WILL DO IT

The following steps will be performed:

- Create the project folder with data and reports subfolders.
- Create the text files for the catalogue and reports.
- Enter 10 sample book records in books.txt.
- Use grep to separate available and issued books.
- Use cut to extract titles and grep to search by title or category.
- Use sort to arrange entries alphabetically by title.
- Use head, tail, and less to view catalogue entries and reports.
- Combine filtered files into one final inventory report.

